From 885eaff443426a3d78e18b32b6084af983023cb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:23:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: move front camera (IMX471) from cci1_i2c0 to cci1_i2c1

The vendor OEM devicetree for this exact device (kona-oem-camera-kebab_t0.dtsi,
qcom,cam-sensor@2 'Front cam: IMX471') specifies cci-master = <1> for both
the front sensor and its EEPROM (eeprom_front_0), within the &cam_cci1 block
(qcom,cci@ac50000 -- confirmed identical to mainline's cci1). In mainline's
i2c-bus@N child-node binding, master index 1 corresponds to i2c-bus@1
(cci1_i2c1, /dev/i2c-24 on kebab), not i2c-bus@0 (cci1_i2c0, /dev/i2c-23,
where the mainline port originally placed it in patch 0059).

With the CCI1 clock rate now correctly pinned to 37.5MHz (patch 0072) and
full driver-mediated power/reset sequencing confirmed correct, the sensor
still fails chip-id reads with -ENXIO on cci1_i2c0/0x1a, while cci1_i2c0
does answer at plausible EEPROM addresses (0x50/0x58) and cci1_i2c1 answers
at different addresses (0x54/0x5c) under a cold (unpowered) scan. Since the
sensor's own power/clock/reset only ever ran against cci1_i2c0 so far, a
cold scan of cci1_i2c1 cannot rule the sensor in or out there -- this patch
tests the vendor-specified bus for real, with full power sequencing active.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index ad2068ad1..c79c705d0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1995,7 +1995,7 @@ csiphy4_front_ep: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
-&cci1_i2c0 {
+&cci1_i2c1 {
 	camf_imx471: camera@1a {
 		compatible = "sony,imx471";
 		reg = <0x1a>;
-- 
2.55.0

